WEBVTT

00:09.780 --> 00:13.280
Keishin Academy
6th Years

00:09.780 --> 00:13.280
Keishin Academy
5th Years

00:10.900 --> 00:13.240
Looks like Aoi found my weakness.

00:13.280 --> 00:14.950
What do you mean?

00:14.950 --> 00:20.040
Our team is at its best with Saki
methodically controlling the ball at point.

00:20.450 --> 00:24.710
Aoi is countering that with the run and gun.

00:24.710 --> 00:26.960
They attack way too fast compared to us.

00:26.960 --> 00:28.090
I see.

00:28.090 --> 00:32.380
They up the pace and shoot as much as they can?

00:32.380 --> 00:35.510
Their field goal percentage isn't half bad, either.

00:35.510 --> 00:36.390
Yeah.

00:36.390 --> 00:41.180
Our rhythm is all messed up so we've fallen for their pace.

00:41.180 --> 00:42.520
They're playing us perfectly.

00:42.980 --> 00:45.020
What will you do, Coach?

00:46.060 --> 00:48.730
Don't worry, I have a plan.

00:52.570 --> 00:55.660
Make them see that halation!

00:55.660 --> 00:59.080
We'll carry out the oath we made that day.

00:59.080 --> 01:02.160
Spread out, new formation!

01:02.160 --> 01:05.620
We can see the signs as we call out for one another.

01:05.620 --> 01:11.920
Place your hopes in it, shoot, and watch the arch!

01:12.210 --> 01:16.840
I believe in you, do it like you always do.

01:16.840 --> 01:18.510
Leave it to me.

01:18.510 --> 01:25.060
Put your hands on your chest, and calm yourself down.

01:25.060 --> 01:31.360
I remember each and every granted wish,

01:31.360 --> 01:37.240
including that day I cried in secret.

01:37.240 --> 01:40.740
We're not the only ones

01:40.740 --> 01:44.290
seeing these same dreams.

01:44.290 --> 01:47.920
The sparks in those unyielding eyes

01:47.920 --> 01:51.040
that appeared in front of me,

01:51.040 --> 01:52.630
let them fly!

01:52.920 --> 01:56.050
Make them see that halation!

01:56.050 --> 01:59.390
Run into that open space!

01:59.390 --> 02:06.020
This lingering sensation, looking back on those carefree days.

02:06.020 --> 02:12.570
After saying farewell, you smile with everyone else,

02:12.570 --> 02:18.860
aim for the place you dreamed of, shoot, and watch the arch!

02:26.290 --> 02:27.960
Good work, everyone.

02:27.960 --> 02:28.870
You're doing great.

02:29.330 --> 02:33.380
Huh? Onii-chan, we're losing.

02:33.380 --> 02:36.960
Well, they've been training very hard, too.

02:36.960 --> 02:38.840
This is a lot different from the last match.

02:38.840 --> 02:41.840
But don't worry. I know how we can win.

02:42.510 --> 02:44.220
That's my Subarun!

02:44.220 --> 02:46.560
So what will we do?

02:50.940 --> 02:54.770
Airi, focus more this half on pressure defense.

02:55.820 --> 02:58.570
Don't roll too far to the basket on offense.

02:58.570 --> 03:01.780
Stand near the free throw line and support your teammates.

03:01.780 --> 03:04.330
When you're on defense, fall back immediately.

03:04.700 --> 03:05.580
Think you can do it?

03:05.580 --> 03:08.540
I-I think I can! I'll do it!

03:08.540 --> 03:09.540
Okay.

03:09.540 --> 03:12.170
Saki, there's one thing you need to do...

03:12.170 --> 03:12.830
Okay!

03:16.250 --> 03:17.170
Everyone!

03:17.170 --> 03:19.590
Just keep on running for the second half!

03:19.590 --> 03:21.590
Okay!

03:22.090 --> 03:25.100
This is a pretty tough strategy.

03:25.100 --> 03:26.390
Can you do it?

03:27.350 --> 03:30.600
It is indeed tough, but let me try!

03:31.310 --> 03:32.810
All right, then.

03:32.810 --> 03:35.310
What's next, Subaru? What's next?

03:35.310 --> 03:38.650
Oh! I'll do my best at whatever, too!

03:38.650 --> 03:42.030
If there's anything I can do to help, please tell me!

03:42.030 --> 03:44.660
You three will play the same way this half.

03:44.660 --> 03:47.370
Huh? We'll depend only on Airin and Saki?

03:48.740 --> 03:54.380
Well, I'd like it if you play a bit harder on offense to help out Airi and Saki.

03:54.380 --> 03:59.710
We'll attack on offense to make up for Airi and Saki playing defense, right?

03:59.710 --> 04:01.010
All right!

04:01.380 --> 04:04.470
But, but! We have to work hard on defense, too.

04:04.470 --> 04:06.680
Attack hard, defend hard!

04:06.680 --> 04:08.640
That's my Subarun! I love simple explanations!

04:12.020 --> 04:14.020
Will you be okay, Saki?

04:14.020 --> 04:17.570
It's a bit tough, but that's what makes it fun, right?

04:17.570 --> 04:19.280
How about <i>you</i>? Will you be okay?

04:19.280 --> 04:20.320
With what?

04:20.320 --> 04:21.530
Offense.

04:21.530 --> 04:24.110
Don't go crazy without me there.

04:24.110 --> 04:25.740
I won't.

04:25.740 --> 04:29.040
I'll do my best so you can do what you gotta do.

04:30.410 --> 04:32.040
All right. I'm expecting the best from you.

04:43.220 --> 04:43.840
Hii!

04:44.510 --> 04:45.220
Gettan!

04:45.550 --> 04:46.510
Nice pass!

04:51.890 --> 04:52.980
Kagetsu!

05:01.650 --> 05:03.240
Awesome!

05:03.240 --> 05:04.150
Nice shot!

05:11.120 --> 05:11.990
Hina-chan!

05:14.910 --> 05:16.420
Take this!

05:17.420 --> 05:19.090
So fast!

05:20.250 --> 05:21.130
Mokkan!

05:31.810 --> 05:34.430
Maho and the others got faster all of a sudden.

05:34.430 --> 05:38.060
They left the offense to three players, so their attacks got simpler.

05:38.060 --> 05:40.190
Naturally their pace went up.

05:40.190 --> 05:44.320
This seems like a simple strategy, but the players are doing it really well.

05:47.450 --> 05:49.320
Keishin Academy
6th Years

05:47.450 --> 05:49.320
Keishin Academy
5th Years

05:48.280 --> 05:49.320
Tsuba!

05:53.620 --> 05:54.950
Masami, here!

06:07.880 --> 06:09.050
I'll leave it to you!

06:16.270 --> 06:17.560
Again?

06:18.350 --> 06:22.020
Masami-chan! You're moving too far away from the basket!

06:22.440 --> 06:25.030
Shoot at a distance where you know you can make it!

06:25.030 --> 06:27.740
Too far away? When did I...

06:35.660 --> 06:39.460
Why isn't Masami shooting from her usual spot?

06:39.460 --> 06:41.920
Saki-chan is pressuring her.

06:41.920 --> 06:42.670
Huh?

06:42.670 --> 06:46.460
Saki-chan's defense seems normal at first.

06:46.460 --> 06:51.180
But she's been forcing Masami-chan to shoot from further away every time.

06:53.300 --> 06:55.930
How can you possibly pressure me?

06:56.770 --> 06:59.690
Mind games are important in basketball too, you know.

06:59.690 --> 07:01.020
I see.

07:01.020 --> 07:03.900
You're having the Airi and Saki duo on defense.

07:03.900 --> 07:08.530
If you only had Airi on defense, the other team would blow by her using their speed.

07:08.530 --> 07:12.780
But I think you could have also gone with an all out attack.

07:12.780 --> 07:17.160
You'd have to watch your pace and it would be a lot easier to mess up.

07:17.750 --> 07:19.830
I feel it's best to attack methodically.

07:19.830 --> 07:22.290
So that's why I wanted to
maintain our usual play style.

07:24.130 --> 07:25.090
Masami!

07:36.220 --> 07:37.390
Masami...

07:37.640 --> 07:40.390
Don't mind me, it's my job to do long shots.

07:42.650 --> 07:43.310
Masami!

07:45.820 --> 07:48.690
<i>Dribbling, defense and pace...</i>

07:48.690 --> 07:50.990
<i>I'm the worst in all those areas on our team.</i>

07:51.740 --> 07:52.990
<i>That's why...</i>

07:53.240 --> 07:55.160
This is all I've got!

08:00.910 --> 08:02.420
Not bad.

08:02.420 --> 08:04.380
You're pretty good, Masami.

08:04.790 --> 08:06.420
Of course I am!

08:06.420 --> 08:09.420
That's the reason I'm on this team.

08:09.420 --> 08:11.170
Keishin Academy
6th Years

08:09.420 --> 08:11.170
Keishin Academy
5th Years

08:20.980 --> 08:23.350
Crap! We won't lose!

08:23.690 --> 08:26.730
Seems like the fifth-years are running out of gas.

08:26.730 --> 08:28.150
Will we win like this?

08:28.730 --> 08:30.150
Or...

08:33.990 --> 08:35.110
Hiiragi!

08:37.160 --> 08:38.410
Gotcha!

08:39.660 --> 08:41.330
It'll be a 4-point difference if they score here!

08:42.710 --> 08:44.120
We've got this!

08:52.300 --> 08:54.260
In the end, it all comes down to...

08:55.050 --> 08:56.800
...the talent of our aces!

08:56.800 --> 08:58.300
I won't let you pass!

08:58.300 --> 09:00.060
I won't lose again!

09:18.620 --> 09:20.950
A turn-around jumper.

09:20.950 --> 09:23.620
That shouldn't be something an
elementary schooler is able to do.

09:25.000 --> 09:26.620
Now it's tied.

09:28.380 --> 09:30.540
Okay! Let's go!

09:31.340 --> 09:32.170
Here!

09:32.170 --> 09:33.840
Oh! Here you go!

09:34.550 --> 09:35.300
Make this, Mo!

09:36.930 --> 09:38.930
We all pitched in to get these points!

09:38.930 --> 09:40.260
I won't let them go to waste!

09:54.610 --> 09:57.030
No! I won't let you shoot!

10:00.990 --> 10:01.950
A long shot?!

10:01.950 --> 10:03.410
No, that's...

10:19.510 --> 10:21.350
Mokkan, you're the best!

10:21.350 --> 10:24.470
You finally perfected your floater!

10:24.470 --> 10:26.270
That was an amazing buzzer beater!

10:26.270 --> 10:29.020
Oh! I was so surprised!

10:40.530 --> 10:42.120
Great work, everyone.

10:42.580 --> 10:43.950
Good game, Subaru.

10:47.120 --> 10:49.000
You were pretty good.

10:49.000 --> 10:51.580
You really pushed us today.

10:51.580 --> 10:52.630
Yeah...

10:53.170 --> 10:56.170
Tomoka-chan and her
teammates were really tough.

10:57.970 --> 10:59.630
First we need to thank you all...

10:59.630 --> 11:00.890
It's not happening!

11:00.890 --> 11:03.760
We're not becoming your underlings, even if we die!

11:03.760 --> 11:08.020
If we have to face such shame, then we'll just quit playing basketball!

11:08.020 --> 11:11.310
That's not true, Tsubaki-chan, Hiiragi-chan!

11:11.310 --> 11:13.480
The sixth-years aren't going to...

11:13.480 --> 11:15.690
You shut up, Aoi-oneesan!

11:15.690 --> 11:17.820
You didn't think of a way for us to win!

11:17.820 --> 11:18.490
You liar!

11:20.950 --> 11:21.990
I'm sorry.

11:24.070 --> 11:28.700
Do you two really think it was because of Aoi-oneesan that you lost?

11:31.250 --> 11:34.340
W-We'll never be your underlings!

11:34.340 --> 11:35.750
We're gonna quit playing basketball!

11:37.340 --> 11:38.550
Wait!

11:38.550 --> 11:42.180
Those two are super stubborn. I'll go after them.

11:43.640 --> 11:46.930
That wasn't cool at all.

11:46.930 --> 11:48.020
Masami.

11:48.680 --> 11:52.060
You were amazing today. Not just your shot, your movements, too...

11:52.060 --> 11:53.600
Silence.

11:53.600 --> 11:56.940
Your words of encouragement just make my anger rise.

11:57.860 --> 11:59.280
Um...

12:05.370 --> 12:06.530
I'm going, too.

12:06.990 --> 12:07.950
Okay.

12:07.950 --> 12:09.700
Thanks, Aoi.

12:09.700 --> 12:12.210
I may be a bit selfish by saying this,

12:12.210 --> 12:13.170
but it was a lot of fun.

12:15.960 --> 12:18.550
Do your best in the finals.

12:25.970 --> 12:27.720
Aoi-chan!

12:28.140 --> 12:29.970
Manaka-senpai...

12:31.310 --> 12:34.980
Aoi, we'll go inside first to get seats.

12:44.360 --> 12:47.320
Being a coach sure is difficult.

12:48.990 --> 12:49.990
Aoi-chan...

12:51.700 --> 12:54.870
These thoughts just keep popping up in my head.

12:54.870 --> 12:58.750
"If only I had done this, or that..."

13:00.000 --> 13:00.750
Yeah.

13:00.750 --> 13:05.130
Maybe they could have won, too...

13:07.340 --> 13:08.600
Yeah.

13:12.980 --> 13:15.980
Miyakoooji Aya

13:12.980 --> 13:15.980
Date of birth

13:12.980 --> 13:15.980
Blood type

13:12.980 --> 13:15.980
Class     Suzuridani Girls School
5th Year, Class 3

13:12.980 --> 13:15.980
Height                   \

13:12.980 --> 13:15.980
Bust size    Quite developed, like her height.

13:12.980 --> 13:15.980
Person she
respects

13:12.980 --> 13:15.980
Kashii Airi

13:21.230 --> 13:23.240
Keishin Academy
6th Years

13:21.230 --> 13:23.240
Suzuridani
Girls School

13:30.580 --> 13:31.450
Mokkan!

13:31.870 --> 13:32.660
Maho!

13:38.260 --> 13:39.880
Wow!

13:39.880 --> 13:41.340
We should be able to win like this.

13:41.340 --> 13:43.760
Yeah, even though they aren't playing with their starters.

13:44.260 --> 13:47.300
They're able to play this well
against such a strong school...

13:47.300 --> 13:49.260
They're really something.

13:57.600 --> 13:58.810
Saki-chan!

13:58.810 --> 13:59.400
Airi...

13:59.810 --> 14:02.520
Pass the ball to me!

14:03.440 --> 14:05.110
Okay! Got it!

14:21.290 --> 14:23.130
Airi-san...

14:26.300 --> 14:28.340
Aya, don't lose her!

14:28.340 --> 14:31.340
You're the only one who can stop Airi-chan!

14:38.140 --> 14:39.230
Okay!

14:39.690 --> 14:44.650
Airi wants to show her how to play as a tall player.

14:49.490 --> 14:50.610
Airi-san.

14:50.610 --> 14:52.030
Here I go, Aya-chan!

14:53.200 --> 14:54.030
Okay!

15:14.050 --> 15:19.390
With a final score of 30 to 18, Keishin Academy's sixth-year girls basketball team wins!

15:19.390 --> 15:21.810
Thank you very much!

15:38.410 --> 15:40.330
One, two!

15:40.330 --> 15:43.710
Yeah! We won!

15:48.590 --> 15:52.340
Let's have a great game next time, with our starters.

15:52.340 --> 15:54.970
Sure, if we can...

15:54.970 --> 15:56.560
No, we <i>will</i> play.

16:01.480 --> 16:03.230
U-Um...

16:03.600 --> 16:08.750
Thanks to you, I've come to love basketball.

16:09.610 --> 16:12.740
Let's both do our best.

16:14.660 --> 16:17.450
Yes, Onee-sama!

16:32.760 --> 16:34.510
See you later!

16:35.760 --> 16:38.140
Bye-bye!

16:41.350 --> 16:44.310
Now then, let's get to the party.

16:44.310 --> 16:47.310
Maho's dad took the time to prepare it.

16:47.310 --> 16:48.570
We shouldn't be late.

16:48.570 --> 16:49.520
Okay!

16:49.520 --> 16:50.530
Subaru!

16:51.940 --> 16:53.780
Aoi, good timing.

16:53.780 --> 16:56.240
Wanna come with us to the party?

16:56.240 --> 16:57.530
About that...

17:06.880 --> 17:11.260
Wow! I didn't expect a simple party to be this grand.

17:11.260 --> 17:12.170
Yeah...

17:12.710 --> 17:16.680
<i>I've already told them I'll miss the party.</i>

17:17.590 --> 17:20.930
<i>I want to go look for Tsubaki-chan and Hiiragi-chan.</i>

17:24.430 --> 17:27.690
Excuse us for the interruption.

17:27.690 --> 17:30.270
Would you all focus your attention on the stage?

17:33.990 --> 17:37.200
This is Fuuga-sama's special present.

17:43.830 --> 17:46.540
Is this our very own uniform?

17:46.540 --> 17:49.880
Yes, we've prepared uniforms for all of you.

17:49.880 --> 17:53.460
Wow! Matching uniforms!

17:53.460 --> 17:55.090
It's like a dream come true!

17:55.090 --> 17:59.590
<i>I want to have them wear that and play in official matches.</i>

18:04.930 --> 18:08.350
Well then, let's get this started!

18:15.650 --> 18:17.360
Beer party!

18:17.360 --> 18:20.320
Y-You can't! No alcohol!

18:20.320 --> 18:27.370
Please do not worry. These are
non-alcoholic beer for children.

18:27.370 --> 18:29.920
N-Non-alcoholic?

18:29.920 --> 18:32.420
Well, just take it easy for once.

18:32.420 --> 18:34.670
You don't get to experience this often.

18:35.260 --> 18:38.300
Miho-nee, you're getting way too excited.

18:38.300 --> 18:39.680
Take this!

18:41.220 --> 18:43.390
How's that shot in the face?

18:43.390 --> 18:44.930
Maho!

18:44.930 --> 18:47.100
Here you go, Subaru-sama.

18:48.440 --> 18:50.020
Let me return the favor!

18:50.520 --> 18:52.270
Subaru, it's so cold!

18:50.850 --> 18:52.270
Stop running!

18:54.270 --> 18:57.440
Go! Double attack!

18:57.440 --> 18:59.490
Wait, my glasses!

18:58.400 --> 19:00.530
Fire!

19:00.530 --> 19:03.280
Hina! You better be ready!

19:04.700 --> 19:06.450
Onii-chan barrier!

19:07.290 --> 19:10.040
O-Onii-chan, here I come!

19:12.210 --> 19:15.300
A-Airi is...

19:17.050 --> 19:18.720
That was pretty fun.

19:26.060 --> 19:27.810
Tomoka? What's the matter?

19:31.600 --> 19:33.610
Shubaru-san?

19:42.360 --> 19:43.490
Tomoka?

19:43.490 --> 19:47.120
Subaru-san, where did you go?

19:47.120 --> 19:50.660
I was so lonely!

19:50.660 --> 19:53.790
Wh-What's the matter, all of sudden?

19:54.420 --> 19:56.800
Don't tell me you got drunk off these?

19:57.420 --> 19:59.760
But they're non-alcoholic...

19:59.760 --> 20:01.800
Subaru-sama...

20:02.300 --> 20:12.810
You must stay by my side forever! Forever and ever!

20:12.810 --> 20:13.600
T-Tomo—

20:16.940 --> 20:22.990
Subaru-san, you smell so nice! I won't let go!

20:31.870 --> 20:34.500
Don't tell me you're regretting it.

20:34.500 --> 20:36.750
W-We're not regretting anything!

20:36.750 --> 20:39.380
Not playing basketball is a lot more relaxing!

20:39.380 --> 20:42.380
Yeah! There's no point if we can't beat Maho!

20:42.760 --> 20:46.140
Basketball wasn't a fit for us from the very beginning.

20:46.140 --> 20:48.720
See? We're so short.

20:48.720 --> 20:52.770
The two of us are invincible, but we can't show our full potential in a five-person team.

20:53.310 --> 20:56.480
Are you two actually being serious?

21:01.190 --> 21:02.780
So funny!

21:02.780 --> 21:06.280
That's what losers should act like.

21:07.780 --> 21:09.450
Who're you?

21:09.450 --> 21:12.870
Is it just me or are you making fun of us?

21:12.870 --> 21:15.120
No, I'm not.

21:15.120 --> 21:20.550
I'm just here to see how a losing team cries.

21:20.880 --> 21:22.960
Wh-What's with you?

21:22.960 --> 21:28.680
We lost the finals and our coach didn't care at all.

21:28.680 --> 21:32.430
I came here because I wanted to see her sorry face.

21:32.430 --> 21:37.270
But seeing your dejected faces made me feel a lot better.

21:38.440 --> 21:43.610
Watch your tongue, midget.
I think you need a little lesson from your elders!

21:43.610 --> 21:46.950
We'll teach you not to mess with fifth-years!

21:47.320 --> 21:49.740
Sure! Come at me!

21:49.740 --> 21:51.950
Want to settle this with basketball?

21:55.620 --> 21:58.380
Rolling! Rolling! Growing!

21:58.380 --> 21:59.920
Rolling! Rolling!

21:59.920 --> 22:02.840
Keep on bouncing!

22:01.130 --> 22:03.840
Rolling! Rolling! Growing!

22:03.840 --> 22:06.260
Elementary schoolers are the best!

22:06.260 --> 22:06.630
Yay!

22:10.720 --> 22:15.730
Our bodies and our hearts are size SS,

22:16.230 --> 22:21.650
but our dreams can be size LL, can't they? Can't they?

22:21.650 --> 22:27.030
Adolescents have lots of troubles,

22:27.030 --> 22:32.620
but we'll overcome them together.

22:32.620 --> 22:38.040
I want to get even better!

22:33.410 --> 22:34.790
Even

22:38.040 --> 22:45.710
I want to see your face when I surprise you!

22:39.000 --> 22:39.440
Ooh!

22:40.330 --> 22:40.720
Wow!

22:45.920 --> 22:48.630
Just keep on spinning!

22:48.630 --> 22:52.550
The Earth is one big basketball!

22:52.550 --> 22:56.220
I'll believe in the future and move forward!

22:55.600 --> 22:57.140
I'll keep going!

22:56.850 --> 22:59.560
Just keep on spinning!

22:59.560 --> 23:03.520
The universe is one big basketball court!

23:03.520 --> 23:06.940
I want you to receive it.

23:06.230 --> 23:07.190
Ready, and!

23:06.940 --> 23:08.780
Pass! Pass! Pass!

23:09.200 --> 23:11.200
Please take it!

23:12.450 --> 23:15.200
Rolling! Rolling! Growing!

23:15.200 --> 23:16.750
Rolling! Rolling!

23:16.750 --> 23:19.620
Keep on bouncing!

23:17.870 --> 23:20.620
Rolling! Rolling! Growing!

23:20.620 --> 23:23.080
Elementary schoolers are the best!

23:23.080 --> 23:23.920
Yay!

23:25.340 --> 23:27.420
Your wild boar powers were pretty scary!

23:27.420 --> 23:28.300
What are you saying?

23:28.300 --> 23:30.050
You're implying I'm a wild boar myself.

23:30.050 --> 23:31.550
That's not what I'm implying at all.

23:31.550 --> 23:33.300
I think it's kinda cute.

23:33.300 --> 23:34.600
Huh? Cute?

23:34.600 --> 23:36.510
Like how a wild boar sniffs using his snout.

23:36.510 --> 23:37.810
Its thick fur, too.

23:36.990 --> 23:40.000
Next episode

23:37.810 --> 23:39.560
Oh, <i>that</i>?
